.\"	$GergiOS: minix-admin.8,v 1.0 2026/07/11 $
.\"
.Dd July 11, 2026
.Dt MINIX-ADMIN 8
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm minix-admin
.Nd unified system administration tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm services
.Op Ar list | status | start | stop | restart
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm system
.Op Ar info | cpu | memory | disk | uptime
.Nm
.Cm network
.Op Ar interfaces | status | stats | route | arp
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm security
.Cm mac
.Op Ar status | enable | disable | rules
.Nm
.Cm security
.Cm caps
.Op Ar list | set
.Op Ar pid Op Ar capability
.Nm
.Cm security
.Cm audit
.Op Ar status | enable | disable | events | stats
.Op Ar limit
.Nm
.Cm dashboard
.Nm
.Cm help
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the unified administration tool for GergiOS.
It provides a consistent interface for managing services, monitoring
system resources, inspecting network state, and managing security.
.Pp
When invoked without arguments,
.Nm
starts an interactive TUI shell with line editing, command history,
and tab completion.
.Pp
The commands are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm services
Service management.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm list
List all system services with their state, endpoint, PID, and uptime.
.It Cm status Op Ar name
Show service status for all services or a specific service.
.It Cm start Ar name
Start a service via RS_UP IPC.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Stop a service via RS_DOWN IPC.
.It Cm restart Ar name
Restart a service (stop + start).
.El
.It Cm system
System monitoring.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm info
Show all system information (hostname, kernel, uptime, CPU, memory, disk).
.It Cm cpu
Show CPU information (model, cores, load, frequency).
.It Cm memory
Show memory usage (total, used, free) with progress bar.
.It Cm disk
Show disk usage for all mounted filesystems.
.It Cm uptime
Show system uptime and load average.
.El
.It Cm network
Network management.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm interfaces
List all network interfaces with type, MAC, IP, MTU, speed, and flags.
.It Cm status Ar name
Show detailed interface information and statistics.
.It Cm stats
Show packet/byte counters for all interfaces.
.It Cm route
Show the routing table with flags and metrics.
.It Cm arp
Show the ARP cache.
.El
.It Cm security
Security management.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm mac status
Show MAC enforcement state, rules loaded, violation count.
.It Cm mac enable
Enable MAC enforcement.
.It Cm mac disable
Disable MAC enforcement (permissive mode).
.It Cm mac rules
List all loaded MAC policy rules.
.It Cm caps list Ar pid
Show effective, permitted, and bounding capabilities for a process.
.It Cm caps set Ar pid Ar capability
Set a capability for a process.
.It Cm audit status
Show audit daemon status (enabled, log open, pending records, total events).
.It Cm audit enable
Enable audit logging.
.It Cm audit disable
Disable audit logging.
.It Cm audit events Op Ar limit
Show recent audit events (default 20, max 100).
.It Cm audit stats
Show audit event statistics by type.
.El
.It Cm dashboard
Start the real-time TUI monitoring dashboard.
The dashboard auto-refreshes every 2 seconds and shows:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Service status (running/stopped with icons)
.It
CPU, memory, and disk usage with progress bars
.It
Network interface count and traffic
.It
MAC enforcement and audit status
.El
.Pp
Dashboard key bindings:
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm q
Quit the dashboard.
.It Cm r
Force immediate refresh.
.It Cm ?
Show help overlay.
.El
.It Cm help
Show usage summary.
.It Cm version
Show version information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/lib/minix-admin -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/minix-admin
Executable binary.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the interactive admin shell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin
.Ed
.Pp
List all services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin services list
.Ed
.Pp
Check memory usage:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin system memory
.Ed
.Pp
Show network interfaces:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin network interfaces
.Ed
.Pp
Show MAC security status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin security mac status
.Ed
.Pp
Open the real-time dashboard:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin dashboard
.Ed
.Pp
Restart the Bluetooth daemon:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
minix-admin services restart bluetoothd
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr auditd 8 ,
.Xr macd 8 ,
.Xr auditctl 8 ,
.Xr macctl 8 ,
.Xr services.conf 5 ,
